From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 23:47:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fbcon: Let an explicit logo count outlive a quiet boot

A quiet command line turns the boot logo off:  fbcon sees
console_loglevel at or below CONSOLE_LOGLEVEL_QUIET and decides the
logo is unwanted.  For a desktop being quietened that is the right
guess, because quiet is about having less to read and the logo is one
more thing on the screen.

On a device whose only console is the panel it is the wrong one, and
there is no way to say so.  The same command line can ask for the logo
by name, with fbcon=logo-count: and fbcon=logo-pos:, and those requests
are then thrown away by a guess made from an unrelated option.  What is
left is a screen that stays black from the moment the loader hands over
until the login prompt appears, on a phone where that is several
seconds and the only sign the system is alive.

So let the guess apply only where nothing was said: a count given on
the command line is already an answer to whether the logo is wanted.
Where no count is given, quiet behaves exactly as before.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c
index 23b3c536d53..48c9780ca1e 100644
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c
@@ -1103,7 +1103,14 @@ static void fbcon_init(struct vc_data *vc, bool init)
 
 	info = fbcon_info_from_console(vc->vc_num);
 
-	if (logo_shown < 0 && console_loglevel <= CONSOLE_LOGLEVEL_QUIET)
+	/*
+	 * A quiet boot asked for less to read, not for no logo.  Where the
+	 * command line names a count of its own, that is already an answer
+	 * to whether the logo is wanted, and this is not the place to
+	 * overrule it.
+	 */
+	if (logo_shown < 0 && console_loglevel <= CONSOLE_LOGLEVEL_QUIET &&
+	    fb_logo_count < 0)
 		logo_shown = FBCON_LOGO_DONTSHOW;
 
 	if (vc != svc || logo_shown == FBCON_LOGO_DONTSHOW ||
